  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Losin' Yo Head**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [4]\n- **Friends Again**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [4]\n- **Move On Up**: rare: 10 archived performances [4]\n- **Mother In Law**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Carnival Time**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2010-04-20.mk4v.flac24** (recommended): source not stated; 24 songs; 143 min [1]\n- **mmj2010-04-20**: source not stated; 24 songs; 143 min [3]. Said about its sound: The recording sounds very nice despite preamp issues during the first band [3]\n- **mmj2010-04-20.mk4v.flac16**: source not stated; 24 songs; 143 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Preservation Hall Jazz Band joined for the final six songs of the encore [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2010-04-20.mk4v.flac24**: taped by Taylor Caine; transferred by taylorc; source: [24bit] Schoeps mk4v> KC5> M222> NT222> Lunatec V3> SD 744t (@24bit/96kHz) [1]\n- **mmj2010-04-20**: taped by willsfc; transferred by MSTaper; source: Church Audio CA-11 (cardoid) > Edirol R-09 (24/48) [3]\n- **mmj2010-04-20.mk4v.flac16**: taped by Taylor Caine; transferred by taylorc; source: [16bit] Schoeps mk4v> KC5> M222> NT222> Lunatec V3> SD 744t (@24bit/96kHz) [2]",
